IMPORT prelude

§ `Codex Insurance Limited -- Hospital Income Policy`

-- This file encodes the substantive coverage rules of the policy contract
-- (see fixtures/chubb-policy.txt) as pure functions of a single hospitalization
-- claim. No claim data is defined in this file -- see apply.l4.
--
-- Two simplifications, both directed by the task brief:
--   * Sec. 1.1(1) "this agreement is signed" and Sec. 1.1(2) "the applicable
--     premium ... has been paid" are assumed always TRUE and are therefore
--     not modelled as fields or conjuncts anywhere below.
--   * Every date/time fact about a claim (other than the claimant's age) is
--     expressed as a plain NUMBER of months elapsed since the policy's
--     effective date, e.g. "5 months after the effective date" becomes the
--     NUMBER 5. There is never a need to difference two calendar dates, so
--     no DATE arithmetic is used anywhere in this file.

§§ `The facts of a single hospitalization claim`

DECLARE Claim HAS
    -- Sec. 3.1(5): the claimant's age, in whole years, at the time of the
    -- hospitalization on which the claim is premised.
    `age at hospitalization` IS A NUMBER

    -- How many months after the policy's effective date the hospitalization
    -- began. Used only to decide whether Sec. 1.3's deadlines have already
    -- come and gone by the time of this hospitalization, and whether the
    -- one-year policy term (Sec. 4.6) has already run out.
    `hospitalization month` IS A NUMBER

    -- Sec. 2.1: TRUE only if the confinement is actually a result of
    -- sickness, or of an *accidental* (i.e. unintended, fortuitous) injury.
    -- A deliberate, self-inflicted act is neither a sickness nor an
    -- accidental injury, so this is FALSE for that case.
    `caused by sickness or accidental injury` IS A BOOLEAN

    -- Sec. 2.2: the Daily Hospital Income Benefit is payable only for
    -- confinement "in a hospital in the United States" -- distinct from
    -- Sec. 4.1.1's promise that the claimant is insured worldwide, which
    -- covers where the sickness/injury may arise, not where the benefit is
    -- payable.
    `hospital is in the United States` IS A BOOLEAN

    -- Sec. 3.1(1)-(4): each of these is TRUE only if the sickness or
    -- accidental injury arose directly or indirectly out of that named
    -- activity. Simply holding the occupation or status at the time of
    -- hospitalization, with no causal link to the hospitalization, does not
    -- make this TRUE.
    `event arose from skydiving` IS A BOOLEAN
    `event arose from service in the military` IS A BOOLEAN
    `event arose from service as a fire fighter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `event arose from service in the police` IS A BOOLEAN

    -- Sec. 1.2: fraud, misrepresentation, or material withholding of
    -- information provided to the Company cancels the policy outright.
    `fraud or misrepresentation occurred` IS A BOOLEAN

    -- Sec. 1.3: how many months after the effective date the wellness visit
    -- itself took place -- NOTHING if, as of this claim, it has not (yet)
    -- taken place.
    `wellness visit month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

    -- Sec. 1.3: how many months after the effective date written
    -- confirmation of the wellness visit was supplied to the Company --
    -- NOTHING if, as of this claim, it has not (yet) been supplied.
    `wellness visit confirmation month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

§§ `Sec. 1.3 -- the wellness-visit condition`

-- "No later than the 7th month anniversary of the effective date of this
-- policy, you will supply us with written confirmation from the medical
-- provider in question of a wellness visit for yourself with a qualified
-- medical provider occurring no later than the 6th month anniversary of the
-- effective date of this policy."
--
-- This is two deadlines, not one: the visit itself must occur by month 6,
-- and confirmation of it must reach the Company by month 7. Either one
-- being missed defeats Sec. 1.3.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `confirmation deadline missed` claim IF
    CONSIDER claim's `wellness visit confirmation month`
    WHEN JUST m  THEN m GREATER THAN 7
    WHEN NOTHING THEN claim's `hospitalization month` GREATER THAN 7
    -- With no confirmation on file yet, the deadline is only "missed" once
    -- we are already past it; before month 7 the condition is still
    -- pending, not failed (Sec. 1.1(3)).

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wellness visit deadline missed` claim IF
    CONSIDER claim's `wellness visit month`
    WHEN JUST m  THEN m GREATER THAN 6
    WHEN NOTHING THEN claim's `hospitalization month` GREATER THAN 6

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `condition 1-3 not satisfied in a timely fashion` claim IF
        `confirmation deadline missed` claim
    OR  `wellness visit deadline missed` claim

§§ `Sec. 1.2 -- cancellation`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy has been canceled` claim IF
        claim's `fraud or misrepresentation occurred`
    OR  `condition 1-3 not satisfied in a timely fashion` claim
    OR  claim's `hospitalization month` GREATER THAN 12
    -- Sec. 4.6: the policy term is one year from the effective date, and
    -- Sec. 1.2 automatically cancels the policy at the end of that term.

§§ `Sec. 1.1 -- policy in effect`

-- Sec. 1.1(1) "this agreement is signed" and Sec. 1.1(2) "the applicable
-- premium ... has been paid" are assumed always TRUE per the task brief.
-- Sec. 1.1(3) "the condition set out in Section 1.3 is still pending or has
-- been satisfied in a timely fashion" and Sec. 1.1(4) "the policy has not
-- been canceled" are exactly the same fact, seen from two directions --
-- Sec. 1.2 already cancels the policy the moment Sec. 1.3 is not satisfied
-- in a timely fashion -- so both are captured by the single
-- `policy has been canceled` test above.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy is in effect at the time of hospitalization` claim IF
    NOT `policy has been canceled` claim

§§ `Sec. 3.1 -- general exclusions`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a general exclusion applies` claim IF
        claim's `event arose from skydiving`
    OR  claim's `event arose from service in the military`
    OR  claim's `event arose from service as a fire fighter`
    OR  claim's `event arose from service in the police`
    OR  claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

§§ `Sec. 2 -- benefits`

-- Sec. 2.3 (a claim must be made, setting out the basis for it) is a
-- procedural filing requirement, not a substantive coverage condition; it
-- is assumed satisfied whenever a claim is being evaluated at all, exactly
-- as with the signature and premium assumptions above. Sec. 2.2's 365-day
-- cap limits how many days of benefit are paid for a single continuous
-- confinement -- it does not switch coverage off, so it is not a conjunct
-- of the boolean decision below.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the benefit is payable` claim IF
        claim's `caused by sickness or accidental injury`
    AND claim's `hospital is in the United States`

§ `Top-level decision`

@export Decide whether a hospitalization claim is covered under the Codex Insurance hospital income policy
@desc The facts of the hospitalization claim being assessed for coverage
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `covered` claim IF
        `policy is in effect at the time of hospitalization` claim
    AND `the benefit is payable` claim
    AND NOT `a general exclusion applies` claim
